# Text is LF on every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says: the shipped SHA-256 manifests (the board packages, the layout,
# reference/) hash these files, and `sha256sum -c` reads an LF manifest, so a CRLF checkout would fail the release checks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The upstream changelog is preserved byte for byte, with the author's own CRLF line endings: it still hashes to the
# value recorded in reference/SHA256SUMS on every platform.
reference/changelog.txt -text

# Binary assets (git detects most of these anyway; listed so a checkout can never rewrite them).
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.woff2 binary
